<!DOCTYPE html>
<%# Layout for the unauthenticated guest review surface.

    Unlike `public_share` (read-only, no JS) this one *does* load the bundle,
    because reviewing means drawing annotations on an image. It still omits the
    app header, sidebar and navigation: a guest is here for one asset set and
    must not be shown a way into the authenticated application.

    csrf_meta_tags is present because, unlike a share page, this surface
    accepts writes. %>
<html lang="<%= I18n.locale.to_s %>">
<head>
  <title><%= content_for(:title) || "Review — Capri DAM" %></title>
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
  <%# A review link is a credential in a URL; it must never reach an index. %>
  <meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow">
  <%= csrf_meta_tags %>
  <%= csp_meta_tag %>
  <link rel="icon" href="/icon.png" type="image/png">
  <%= stylesheet_link_tag "application", "data-turbo-track": "reload" %>
  <%# The guest bundle only, never "application": that one ships the whole
      internal UI and would boot navigation a guest cannot follow. %>
  <%= javascript_include_tag "guest_review", "data-turbo-track": "reload", defer: true %>
</head>
<body style="margin:0; padding:0; background:#f4f7fb; font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, sans-serif;">
  <header style="background:#fff; border-bottom:1px solid #e2e8f0; padding:14px 24px; display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:space-between;">
    <strong style="font-size:1.05rem; color:#121926;">Capri DAM</strong>
    <span style="font-size:0.75rem; color:#94a3b8; text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:0.05em;">Guest review</span>
  </header>
  <%= yield %>
</body>
</html>
